WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.980
This is still just the second puzzle.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.260
Not being able to solve even
this level of puzzle...

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.950
That really is pathetic.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.700
Here!

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.080
<i>Puzzle Kingdom:</i>

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.170
<i>A stunning palace of
puzzles where the flowers</i>

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.170
<i>
of glory and ruin are in full bloom.</i>

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.960
<i>Let's review the puzzles once more.</i>

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.090
<i>There are eighteen Erena
figurines in three colors.</i>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.050
<i>They must be lined up in a row such that
the colors do not repeat.</i>

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.930
<i>When the arrows are seen from
their respective sides,</i>

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>the color of the first figurine seen
will be displayed as a hint.</i>

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.540
<i>Challengers must use this to infer
the figurines' positions.</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.150
<i>However, the two servant
figurines obstruct the hints.</i>

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.960
<i>Today, the man taking on Queen Erena Himekawa's
puzzle is Naoki Takeda.</i>

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.650
<i>Can he do what no one
has yet accomplished</i>

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.740
<i>and open the door to the
ten-million-yen winner's prize?!</i>

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.400
This! This is in the way!

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.830
I don't get it.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.470
What should I do?!

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.130
It can't be helped.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.110
I will move the servant figurines.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.060
Really?

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.010
However!

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.140
You will get on your knees and say,
"Please, Mistress Erena."

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.150
If you don't, I won't move them.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.420
Erena! Erena! Erena! Erena!

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.620
Mr. Takeda, fight...

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.490
on...

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.880
Please, Mistress Erena.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.050
You're an idiot, aren't you?

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.530
There's no way I'd give you a hint!

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.060
A moron who can't realize that

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.030
isn't worthy of challenging my puzzle.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.060
You fail.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.470
F...

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.240
<i>Naoki Takeda has been eliminated.</i>

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.070
<i>His ten-million-yen dream is shattered!</i>

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.860
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.590
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.440
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.180
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.690
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:00.400
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.620
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.270
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.280
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.580
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.520
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.340
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.840
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.140
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:25.830
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.050
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.390
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.020
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:38.910
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.590
Brain diver

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.390
Brain diver

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.000
Welcome to the Queen's Country

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.620
Erena Himekawa sure is cool.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.170
What's with you, Kaito?

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.790
That's the sort of thing you like, is it?

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.220
Oh, really?

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.480
After I solved this girl's puzzle,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.810
I couldn't get her out of my head.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.270
Why is that?

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.650
I, Ana, think that it's love.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.280
A fourteen-year-old genius starlet, huh?

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.070
What's more, she's everywhere,
on TV shows and commercials...

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:29.990
What a beautiful young girl!

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.790
I'd like to meet her just once.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.870
I wanna have fun with her
and talk about puzzles.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.840
That girl is unacceptable!

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.260
You've been going on about Erena this and

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.360
Erena that recently, so I did some searching.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.840
That girl has some personality problems!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.020
Look.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.970
Having a ten-year career when she's

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.710
still just fourteen is commendable,

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.030
but she'll blow off her TV shows
to go walk around town.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.250
She turns down work she doesn't care for.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.530
She's famous in the industry
for being a selfish diva!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.910
Whoa, sure enough, that's
the scent of a bad woman.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.280
But...

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:12.290
I, Ana, think this girl
seems a little sad.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.870
She seems sad? Really?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.490
In any case, if you got near this girl,

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.560
my precious Kaito would be wounded!

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.790
It's absolutely not allowed!

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.050
There's no way I could get near her.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.720
I apply for Puzzle Kingdom every week,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.760
but I ain't never won once.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.100
Huh? You've been applying every week?!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.850
You like this girl that much?

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.560
Rather, who you've been trying to get

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.560
close to has nothing to do with me...

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.130
Right, Gammon?

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.190
Huh? Where's Gammon?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.230
The video arcade.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.820
He's been obsessed with
winning prizes recently.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.250
Is that so?

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.160
Gammon doesn't have much of a presence,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.160
so I didn't notice he wasn't here.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.380
Someone talkin' about me?

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.790
Keep your eyes on the screen, Galileo.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.880
Whoever loses a hundred times

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.580
has to leave, that's the rule.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.420
You haven't forgotten that, have you?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.180
Shaddup!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:08.720
I can win even if I'm
lookin' away, Antoinette!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.010
How 'bout these apples?

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.390
Getting cocky?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.520
The gloves are off!

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.100
What do you think of this?

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:19.940
Went that route, did you?

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.530
Awesome!

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:24.270
Galileo and Antoinette...

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.780
They both have 99 wins and 99 losses.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.780
Will this finally decide
their turf battle?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.820
Fine! How about this?!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.410
Galileo's on the ropes, huh?

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.580
It seems you'll be the
one to leave this arcade.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.750
You think so?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.050
This is the end.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.620
What are you doing?!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.130
Just come on!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.290
After them! Follow them!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.770
I'm sorry, Erena got away.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.140
What are you doing?!

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.740
Recording is about to begin.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.030
Hurry up and get her!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.440
Looks like they're gone.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.790
Hey, let go of me already!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.440
Now look here!

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.750
That's no way to treat
the guy who saved ya!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.750
Who are those punks anyway?

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.220
Associates of mine.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:28.620
"Associates"?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.130
More importantly, what was the

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.340
meaning of that just now? You coward!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.210
Wh..Who're you callin' a coward?!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.280
Claiming to have "saved" me...

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.320
The truth is, you were afraid of losing
so you threw in the towel!

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.820
Fool, that ain't it!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.810
Then, why would you help me,

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.560
a complete stranger and someone

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.360
you know absolutely nothing about?!

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.780
W..Well, that is...

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.180
Fine, fine, because you're a comrade.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.740
Anyone who does puzzles
is a comrade of mine.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.870
That is why I humbly
assisted you, O Princess.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.440
Don't screw with me!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.710
Who are you calling a
"comrade"? What rubbish!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.200
Aren't you ashamed saying
something like that?

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.500
You're a phony!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.070
Miss Erena!

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.840
I'm coming, shut up already!

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.500
Miss Erena, great work today!

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.750
Excellent work.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.380
Being a celebrity is hard
work, isn't it, Antoinette?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.760
Chief!

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.760
What are you doing here?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.760
You are one of the POG's foremost Givers,

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:02.230
and there is someone I want to attempt
your Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.390
This is...

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:10.400
Initially, I thought it would be enough
to eliminate just Kaito Daimon,

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:13.400
but he has comrades.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.060
"Comrades"?

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.420
They assist Kaito Daimon at every turn.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.160
They are such obstacles.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.700
Yes...

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.060
Let them receive the baptism
that is your puzzle.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.670
Such beautiful fear...

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.710
You are the one most suited for this.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.250
Will you do as I ask?

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.870
Of course.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.180
Hey, Gammon, you're not
going to the arcade today?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.070
Nah, I quit that.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.130
You made too much money and
they banned you from the place?

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.480
That ain't it.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.440
I ran into a kinda troublesome girl.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.140
A troublesome girl?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.580
Nice to see you.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.960
Hey, it's Antoinette!

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.510
That's friggin' Erena Himekawa!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.270
No way, for real?!

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.820
Who's Erena Himekawa?

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.180
I had fun yesterday, Galileo.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.140
I never thought I'd meet a man who

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.190
would hold me tight and not let go.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.650
Kaito, come on.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.420
What the heck?

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.360
Get a clue and come on!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.820
Um, let me have you autograph, please!

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.070
You've got it wrong!
Don't get a clue!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.740
Are they your friends?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.930
Hell, no.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.600
Just some dumbasses I'm stuck with.

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:47.790
It's a love letter! A love letter!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.040
That's a love letter, right? Right?!

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.510
Gammon, you're quite the stud, huh?!

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:05.690
You got it wrong, Nonoha.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.270
Jeez, gimme a friggin' break.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:28.000
I can't believe Erena
Himekawa is a POG Giver.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.610
She sure can make a good puzzle though.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:34.310
Huh? You liked her puzzles?

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:36.500
What else did you think it was?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.960
Thank goodness.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.420
For what, dammit?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.500
Oh, nothing.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.510
Well? How long will we
be kept waitin' here?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.210
We're supposed to go in from there, huh?

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.340
That's the entrance to a TV station!

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.280
Kaito, she's a genius
who's gone up against me.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.530
She may be a celebrity,
but don't sell her short.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.030
She'll hang your ass
out to dry in a second.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.000
I'm gonna solve her puzzle.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.080
That's it.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:10.770
Let's go.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.460
Fine by me.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.520
Kaito Group

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:18.530
- No Smoking
- No Food or Drinks
- No Dangerous Articles
Don't Bring Things in With You
Close the door all the way!

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:29.430
Puzzle Kingdom's stage set is awesome!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.530
Welcome to Puzzle Kingdom!

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.110
A stunning palace of puzzles where

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.520
the flowers of glory and ruin are in full bloom.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.030
I, your queen, shall entertain you with

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.280
the most excellent of puzzles.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.410
Incredible, it's the same
as watching it on TV.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.660
Well, where's the Philosopher's Puzzle?!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.870
Don't be so impatient.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.290
Come on, have a seat.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.750
What's it over there for?

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.460
It must mean something.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.240
I'm gonna go solve it!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.510
I'll go up front and get Antoinette
to focus her anger on me.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.540
Well, I'll stay back here...

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.180
What the heck is this?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.940
Well, let's start the show.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.910
Hey, let me go!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.370
What the...

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.650
Hey, what are you doin', Antoinette?!

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:51.320
What's going on? I can't see from here.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.960
Nonoha, don't look down.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:53.890
You'll regret it.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.020
This is...

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:01.300
I'll have you challenge Puzzle
Kingdom's final stage.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.690
You know the rules, right?

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:06.490
Line the figurines up
according to the arrows.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.570
But the three servant figurines
are covering up the hints.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.410
Servant?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.720
Wait, you mean us?!

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:16.580
In addition, there is a
special rule this time:

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.790
If the servants prevent you
from solving the puzzle,

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.420
try pushing that button.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.420
If you do...

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:37.350
Just like that, the hint
will become visible.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:41.360
This is my Philosopher's Puzzle!

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.710
And the prize is behind that door:

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.610
to the winner goes ten million yen.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:50.950
You used a Philosopher's Puzzle to
get your program aired?!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:51.990
Yes!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.580
But the challengers have
been of such poor level that

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.100
none of them have reached the final puzzle.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.560
It looks like you all
will be my first victims.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.010
You won't get away with this!

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:03.460
Your time limit is five minutes.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.300
When five minutes pass,
the floor will open up

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.300
and you'll all plunge straight to Hell.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:10.980
Screw you!

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:13.010
We're supposed to just
sit and do nothing?!

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.030
Not at all.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.930
I've prepared something interesting

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.270
to keep you from being bored.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.900
If you want to sacrifice
yourself to help your "comrade"

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.960
move forward, just push that button.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:24.490
The floor beneath you will open.

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:28.490
But if you want to survive,
close that panel.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.930
Then Kaito Daimon will fall,
and the show will be over.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.280
Otherwise, Kaito will make
you fall, and you'll die.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:36.850
Wait just a second!

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.350
I will accept no objections.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.650
A queen's word is absolute.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:44.340
So, with ten million yen and
your friends' lives on the line,

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.130
it's puzzle time, let's start!

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.650
Taking such troublesome companions and
using them against him like this...

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.430
Well done, Antoinette.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.270
This exquisite puzzle outstrips that
of any previous Giver.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:08.780
And now, meet your unseemly
end, Kaito Daimon!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.360
Fill spaces the figurines
can't be placed in with Xs:

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.490
that's the way to solve this puzzle!

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.490
The red in this column can only go here.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.330
Which makes the X go here.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:25.970
So this is blue.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.950
She put the chair right
in the frickin' way!

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:36.510
You could see the hint if
you sacrificed your friend.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:37.970
Shut up!

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.230
Blue goes here.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.480
Dammit!

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.140
But the next one...

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.000
Where does the next one go?!

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.620
Well, you'd better resign yourselves.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.080
Right, Galileo?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:09.380
Now that Kaito's back
is against the wall,

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.590
he'll push the button and
you'll fall into the abyss.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:14.110
No, he won't! Kaito wouldn't do that!

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:15.360
He would!

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:19.390
People look out for themselves.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.430
Faith in others is a lie!

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.230
To save their own skins,
they would soon betray anyone:

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.920
friends, you name it!

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:28.020
Bitch...

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.210
What the hell are you after?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.860
I just want to show you how easily faith

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.990
in others can come crashing down.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.000
Well, Galileo? Close that panel.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.080
Prove to me that your own life is more

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.460
important than that of your friends!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.210
Sorry 'bout this, Nonoha!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.350
Gammon, no!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.680
Don't tell me, you intend
to drop yourself!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.390
This was the only way I could think of.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.250
Stop it, Gammon!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.870
I won't fall. I won't drop y'all, either!

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.540
Don't go jumpin' the gun!

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.710
Where do you get off,
trying to sound cool?

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.160
You're out of time.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.010
Fine, then the only thing is...

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.990
to wait a little longer, huh?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.580
Erena, sweetie, there ain't no way I'd go

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.180
with the choices you lined up for us.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:30.330
I'll go with door number
three, thank you.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.290
Kaito, hurry up and solve it!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.760
That's right, Kaito.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:36.840
Solve this thing already.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.680
There will be no falling
or making us fall today!

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.610
A..Are you idiots?

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:44.930
You think you can keep talking
like naïve children?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.320
<i>We're all right, right?</i>

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.290
<i>Kaito...</i>

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.230
Those two columns in the center...

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.420
From the top, they'd both
go blue, yellow, red

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.580
and blue, yellow and red.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:20.020
Blue could go anywhere from
the first to the fourth row...

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:23.010
But there's already blue in the
second and third row,

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.200
which means...

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:26.470
There are two possible patterns!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.980
Which is it? Which is it?

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:32.450
Which one's the answer?!

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.360
At this rate, all three
of them will fall!

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:47.330
There's no more time.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.960
Why won't it stop?!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:55.170
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:58.940
Such conduct is unforgivable in a Giver.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.590
We shall watch the Solvers to the end.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:05.130
That is our role, is it not?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.310
There are two possibilities.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:17.070
If it's not this column,
and it's the other one,

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.320
the third-from-the-bottom
row would have two yellows.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.950
Meaning, this is the right answer.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.070
I see it now.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.460
Solved it.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.510
That's a couple years off my life.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.990
My puzzle...

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.110
It lost.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:07.830
Even Antoinette failed?!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.240
Damn you, Kaito Daimon!

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.530
I totally believed you
could do it, Kaito!

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:21.130
I'm sure I could've
solved it faster though.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.630
Comrades...

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.730
Bastard, you sure put the pressure on me.

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:31.390
Antoinette...

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:35.140
Earlier, when it looked like those
guys were kidnapping you,

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.810
I really did want to help you.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.410
Woot-woot! Chase after her, Gammon!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.930
Then confess your feelings, Gammon!

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:51.910
Wrong! You got it all wrong!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.120
Let's go home.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.920
Dagnabbit!

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.660
Wait, why am I using a country-ism?!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.280
What do you want?

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.220
Let me see Erena Himekawa!

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.150
If you're after an autograph, forget it.

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:08.490
That ain't it!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.720
I haven't gotten that
ten-million-yen prize,

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:12.750
even though I cleared Puzzle Kingdom's final stage!

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:14.680
Oh, ten million yen, is it?

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.270
That sure is something.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.710
You don't believe me, do you?!

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.070
I really did!

00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:20.490
Say it all you like,

00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.350
but it won't get you in to see Erena.

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:24.170
I'm tellin' you, I ain't even a fan!

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:30.170
Gimme my ten million yen!

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.490
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.410
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:52.040
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:57.090
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.570
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:07.930
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.360
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.700
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.380
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.290
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:33.860
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:39.160
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:44.440
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.980
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:58.920
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:05.340
It turns out we'll be appearing in

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:06.620
the TV show Erena stars in!

00:24:06.620 --> 00:24:07.970
How fun!

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:09.920
I want to play a vice shogun

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:12.840
who goes around
the country righting wrongs.

00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:15.300
"Can you not see this family crest?!"

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.390
I, Ana, will play helper to

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.810
someone who witnesses crimes everywhere!

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.900
Next time: "The Queen Strikes Back"

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:27.170
The Queen Strikes Back

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:26.540
What we're saying and these
visuals don't match at all!
